Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here's a simple example of an if/then statement in C:

if (age >= 18) {
    // do something the adult
} else if (age == 13) {
    // do something with a teenager

    // do something with a child
}

In this example, the if statement checks if the person's age is greater than or equal to 18. If it is, the program will execute the body of the if statement (the code inside the curly braces). If it's not, the program will move on to the else if block, where it will check if the person's age is equal to 13. If it is, then the program will execute the body of the else if statement.
